{"accepted_at": "2026-09-23T18:51:40Z", "accepted_evidence": "CVE-2024-6387, also known as RegreSSHion, is a high-severity vulnerability found in OpenSSH servers (sshd) running on glibc-based Linux systems. It is a regression of a previously fixed vulnerability (CVE-2006-5051), which means the issue was reintroduced in newer versions of OpenSSH.", "accepted_reason": "desc_contains_target_only", "cve_id": "CVE-2006-5051", "owner": "anhvutuan", "repo": "CVE-2024-6387-poc-1", "revoked_at": "2026-09-24T07:49:58Z", "revoked_from": "accepted", "revoked_reason": "desc_mention_with_url_conflict", "rule_version": "1", "source": "legacy_markdown", "url": "https://github.com/anhvutuan/CVE-2024-6387-poc-1", "verification": "needs_review"}
